newly released documents about former  Trump campaign advisor Carter page show  how the FBI decided to wiretap him much  of the information is blacked out but  the FBI claims page was targeted for  recruitment by Russia's government page  denies it saying he has never been an  agent of a foreign power the president  and his defenders say the FBI did not  disclose that the wiretap warrant was  based on information from a political  source but the new release shows the FBI  did list the source of the information  Paula Reid is at the Justice Department  Paula what did we learn from this FISA  application all of the evidence that the  government presented to the FISA Court  when it wanted to surveil Carter page  and in this application they refer to  him as a quote agent of a foreign  government and they say that they  believe there was an active campaign by  the Russian government to recruit him as  a spine as you noted Paige has denied  all of these allegations what was also  interesting in this 400 page application  was that this really undercuts  Republican claims that the FBI abused  its surveillance power and failed to  disclose the origins of the so-called  steel dossier that research that was  done on President Trump and his campaign  because if you look at this application  there's over a page long explanation of  the steel dossier and its origins and  the fact that it may have been supported  with some by someone with an anti-trump  bias now also interesting is that the  four judges who approve this  surveillance they were all appointed by  Republican presidents  all right Paul one other question  slightly different matters is the  Michael Cohen the president's lawyer was  apparently who I recorded a conversation  he had with the president what do we  know about that well we know this  recording lasted several minutes about  two two or so minutes and we know that  he and the president discussed a payment  to former Playboy model Karen McDougal  but what we don't know is whether or not  this discussive payment that was  actually saved to her we also don't know  why Cowan chose to record this  conversation but it appears that by  discussing it the president's lawyers  have waived any privilege that he could  have claimed thanks Paul
 

